<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Johann Ludwig Krapf</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1810">1810</a>–<a href="/years/1881">1881</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Johann Krapf</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Johann Ludwig Krapf was a German missionary of the Church Missionary Society who founded the first Protestant mission in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-africa">East Africa</a> at Rabai near Mombasa in 1846. He travelled inland, visiting the Shambaa court, and in 1849 became the first European to see Mount Kenya. He compiled pioneering works on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swahili">Swahili</a> and other East African languages.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/johann-ludwig-krapf.jpg" alt="Johann Ludwig Krapf" width="320" height="398" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Johann_Ludwig_Krapf.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
